      "supports_or_contradicts": "case15: The six JCM originals spell D-Glucose; the doubled source hyphen is punctuation and does not remove D stereochemistry. Current CHEBI17634 explicitly defines D-glucose and includes D(+)-glucose synonyms. Existing D-glucose is the matching D-specific owner.; case41: The successfulTogoM2287 JSON recipe explicitly names D(+)glucose22mM and labels itD-Glucose. CHEBI17634 is the current D-glucose target and the matching maintained owner isD-glucose. This supplies primary confirmation beyond punctuation matching.",
