  "reasoning": "The supplier explicitly specifies D glucose; the positive-rotation spelling is consistent with the captured ChEBID-glucose term and its D(+)-glucose naming. The proposed target was already CHEBI:17634, and the current owner uses D-Glucose with canonical ontologylabel D-glucose. Changing only component_name to D-glucose therefore expresses the existing identity using an accepted label. The native partonomy validator normalizes Unicode, case and whitespace but does not remove punctuation; D(+)Glucose lacks the hyphen of the stored supplier-style synonym, so it fails the exact normalized label set. The canonical label resolves without broadening to generic glucose or narrowing to an unstated anomer/hydrate.",
